**Theorem IP7.** With $\varphi_{\rm E}$ denoting Euler's totient,

$$
\mathcal C_n\equiv3^{\varphi_{\rm E}(n)}\Phi_n(1)\pmod5,
\qquad
\chi(\mathcal C_n)=
\begin{cases}
\chi(\ell),&n=\ell^a\text{ for a prime }\ell,\ a\ge1,\\
1,&n\text{ has at least two distinct prime factors}.
\end{cases}                                      \tag{IP7}
$$

